# 13. Risks, Constraints & Assumptions

## 13.1 Risks and Constraints

| Risk / Constraint                                   | Impact | Likelihood     | Mitigation                                                                                  |
| --------------------------------------------------- | ------ | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Limited hackathon build time (3–4 weeks)**        | High   | High           | Freeze Must-have scope early and defer Should/Could features.                               |
| **No live payment/payout provider**                 | Medium | High by design | Use sandbox/simulated payment and document the production integration path separately.      |
| **Rider or business no-show during demonstration**  | Medium | Medium         | Rehearse using seeded demo data and maintain a scripted fallback path.                      |
| **Catalogue data becoming stale or incorrect**      | Medium | Medium         | Track `last_updated`, validate availability, and flag mismatches for administrative review. |
| **Unauthorized access to admin/business functions** | High   | Low–Medium     | Enforce server-side RBAC and complete access-control testing before demonstration.          |

## 13.2 Assumptions

1. The MVP is a working prototype for the hackathon, not a production logistics deployment.
2. Test users have internet access and a modern web browser.
3. Businesses and riders participating in the demonstration will be represented by prepared test/demo accounts.
4. Naira delivery-fee values and search-radius parameters are configurable placeholders and do not represent final commercial pricing.
5. Production payment, payout, logistics, and regulatory requirements will be addressed separately from the hackathon MVP.

